id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "303 and 1293 are connected when time is ignored (both attach to the dense 28/1583 hub core), and the window carries high, rising activity. But no time-respecting chain exists: with the 600-unit relay limit 303 reaches only 10 nodes and never 1293, and even with unlimited waiting it reaches 85 nodes without touching 1293 \u2014 the ordering of edges, not the delay budget, blocks the cascade. The reverse direction fails likewise, and both endpoints have only 4 sparse, temporally scattered events. Conclusion: no genuine cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Static connectivity exists** \u2014 303 sits one hop from hub 1583 (step_13) and 1293 receives from hub 28 (step_06); the 2-hop neighbourhood of 303 (step_05) is a dense hub-dominated blob, so an order-ignoring path clearly exists. The window is also busy overall (8,360 events, 1,969 active nodes; step_02) and increasingly so over time (step_14), with 28 and 1583 being top hubs (step_16). None of that is decisive.\n\n**Temporal evidence is negative:**\n- With the required \u0394 \u2264 600 relay constraint, 303 reaches only 10 nodes and 1293 is not among them (step_01); no path enumerated (step_08).\n- Relaxing the gap to 5,000 grows the horizon to 53 nodes but still fails (step_17); with **no** waiting-time limit at all, 303 reaches 85 nodes and still never 1293 (step_04). So the failure is due to edge *ordering*, not merely the 600-unit budget.\n- Reverse direction also fails (step_11), so it isn't an orientation artefact.\n- Both endpoints are sparse (4 events each, step_03) and their activity is scattered thinly across the window with no temporal co-location (step_09), leaving no opportunity for a prompt relay; the few incident triangles (step_12) do not bridge them.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_dc3dfaa5\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [303, 1293],\n  \"window\": [28296, 66695],\n  \"confidence\": 0.89,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"303 and 1293 are connected when time is ignored (both attach to the dense 28/1583 hub core), and the window carries high, rising activity. But no time-respecting chain exists: with the 600-unit relay limit 303 reaches only 10 nodes and never 1293, and even with unlimited waiting it reaches 85 nodes without touching 1293 \u2014 the ordering of edges, not the delay budget, blocks the cascade. The reverse direction fails likewise, and both endpoints have only 4 sparse, temporally scattered events. Conclusion: no genuine cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 52041, "total_output_tokens": 4076, "total_tokens": 56117, "total_latency_ms": 57833, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}